@startuml PTrack-ERD
hide methods
hide stereotypes

title PTrack v0.1.0 — Entity-Relationship Diagram

entity "Project" as Project {
  *id : UUID <<PK>>
  --
  name : String [NOT NULL, max 100]
  description : String [NULLABLE, max 250]
  createdAt : Date [NOT NULL]
  stage : Enum [NULLABLE]
  status : Enum [NULLABLE]
}

note right of Project
  stage values (ADR-009):
  Planning | Analysis | Design |
  Implementation | Testing | Done
  -- null when no stage assigned --

  status values (ADR-009, derived from stage):
  No status set (stage = null)
  Not Started   (stage = Planning)
  In Progress   (stage = Analysis | Design |
                          Implementation | Testing)
  Completed     (stage = Done)
  -- stored in localStorage alongside stage --

  name: unique (case-insensitive, spaces ignored)
  (ADR-010)
end note

storage "localStorage" as LS <<browser>>

Project ..> LS : serialised as JSON\n(atomic write, all attributes)

note bottom of LS
  Mechanism: browser localStorage (ADR-003)
  Serialisation: JSON / ISO 8601 dates
  Scope: v0.1.0 single local user
  Future: migrate to centralised DB in Release 0.2
end note

@enduml
